Your thought is correct. I had thought of it as being a "temporary
solution" sort of thing, where you put off fighting someone until a
later date.   Besides the pyrotechnic effects of seeing, e.g., Pakka
Pakka being dragged kicking and screaming into the bowels of hell.

I don't think it's going to be much help on an ascension run.   Reason:
It doesn't work on the planes or in Gehennom.   That leaves a VERY
narrow window in the ascension run (between the castle and level 1)
where it could be valuable.

I typically encounter Rodney 5-7 times during the run.  5 times or so
in Gehennom (thank you, #$%#$%#$ Mysterious force!) , once in the
Mazes, and once on the plane of earth.

So I personally wouldn't waste the weight by carrying a wand of
banishment during the run.   Not if I have a wand of death.

This does bring up a good idea, though ... bring back the more
spectacular killed enemies from the Mazes in Gehennom during the course
of the game.  After all, where are they most likely to go when they
die, anyway?    Then randomly regenerate both them and named demons on
a Gehennom level after they've been killed  every couple thousand (ten
thousand? twenty thousand?) turns or so.

Not only would it make Gehennom more challenging, it would also
discourage some of the more dramatic forms of abuse.  Are you really
going to spend thousands of turns pudding farming, when there's a very
real chance that doing so means you'll have to face Juiblex and Orcus
again?  Possibly together?  

